<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Thuringian Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1247">1247</a>–<a href="/years/1264">1264</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Thuringian Succession of 1247–1264 followed the death without heirs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-raspe">Henry Raspe</a>, the last Ludowingian landgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-margrave-of-meissen">Henry the Illustrious</a>, Margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a>, fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophie-of-brabant">Sophie of Brabant</a>, daughter of Landgrave Louis IV, for the inheritance. The settlement gave Thuringia to the Wettins of Meissen, while Sophie's son Henry I kept the western lands as the new Landgraviate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>.</p></div>
